<title>UK: Commerzbank sets 250 million guilder six-year bond.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank sets 250 million guilder six-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett.</p>
<p> BORROWER   COMMERZBANK OVERSEAS FINANCE NV</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  COMMERZBANK AG</p>
<p> AMT    250 MLN DFL   COUPON     5.00	MATURITY    10.JUN.03</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.19    PAY DATE    10.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    99.615    SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    AMSTERDAM PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 5-20	SALE LIMITS US/DE/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.30	SELL CONC  1.575     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.50 PCT DSL DUE APR.03</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
